WEBVTT

00:00:12.710 --> 00:00:15.090
Well, let's get this day started!

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:02.700
Episode 15
"Honeymoon Over a Silent Ocean"

00:01:06.050 --> 00:01:08.300
<i>I was happy and content.</i>

00:01:09.170 --> 00:01:12.310
<i>So much so that I didn't mind if 
this was the end of my journey.</i>

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:14.580
<i>But...</i>

00:01:15.980 --> 00:01:17.810
<i>Kagari's journey is far from over.</i>

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:20.000
<i>The more her research progresses,</i>

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:23.010
<i>the more worn down she becomes, 
and I can't stop her.</i>

00:01:24.170 --> 00:01:25.410
<i>So the least I can do</i>

00:01:26.790 --> 00:01:28.640
<i>is learn about the world she lives in.</i>

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:36.700
<i>Super-dense information can 
easily fry the human mind,</i>

00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:40.190
<i>so I rewrite and enhance them...</i>

00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:43.480
<i>Not my physical abilities, but my 
awareness and comprehension.</i>

00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:03.130
Love is dependent on the hormone 
secretions humans call emotions

00:02:03.130 --> 00:02:04.520
and is a primeval facet of culture.

00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:06.240
In Kardashev's Type I civilizations,

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:08.430
love acts as an unquestionable 
moral compass.

00:02:08.430 --> 00:02:10.440
As such, studying love's proliferation 
rate in a civilization

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:13.190
allows one to accurately 
estimate how advanced it is.

00:02:13.190 --> 00:02:16.070
In Earth humans' culture, love 
tends to be regarded as sacred,

00:02:16.070 --> 00:02:17.610
but it is essentially just...

00:02:17.610 --> 00:02:19.320
Don't say it!

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:22.850
<i>So cold...</i>

00:02:22.850 --> 00:02:24.070
<i>I didn't know increased knowledge</i>

00:02:24.070 --> 00:02:26.370
<i>could make a person feel so isolated.</i>

00:02:26.900 --> 00:02:31.450
<i>Advanced intelligence exposes even 
human emotions in a cold, stony manner.</i>

00:02:31.630 --> 00:02:33.860
<i>It results in the abandoning of</i>

00:02:33.860 --> 00:02:36.630
<i>the warm feeling of caring for a loved one.</i>

00:02:46.360 --> 00:02:47.450
What should I do?

00:02:47.910 --> 00:02:51.730
I just want to go wherever you go.

00:02:54.820 --> 00:02:58.570
I think I've changed in a lot of minor ways,

00:02:58.570 --> 00:03:00.530
but I'm pretty sure my 
core is still the same.

00:03:01.020 --> 00:03:02.660
So I'm gonna go.

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:14.750
<i>Standing far above the sky, on a plane 
that exists above space and time,</i>

00:03:15.170 --> 00:03:17.990
<i>I could see everything in the universe.</i>

00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:23.410
<i>I understand so much now.</i>

00:03:23.810 --> 00:03:27.510
<i>Wow, there are so many things 
yet to be discovered.</i>

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:28.430
<i>However...</i>

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:31.470
<i>I haven't reached the 
world Kagari lives in yet.</i>

00:03:42.510 --> 00:03:46.700
<i>Powers and laws that nobody 
knows about pique my curiosity.</i>

00:03:47.470 --> 00:03:49.560
<i>But, even so,</i>

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:51.310
<i>I still can't see the summit or Kagari.</i>

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:55.580
<i>I need to go much, much higher.</i>

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:26.070
<i>I'm amazed...</i>

00:04:26.070 --> 00:04:29.560
<i>I never expected the concept of 
love to exist on a plane this high.</i>

00:04:30.050 --> 00:04:33.750
<i>And here I thought it was a base 
emotion, an illusion of the mind.</i>

00:04:36.250 --> 00:04:38.040
<i>Love was once at the very apex of life,</i>

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:40.290
<i>and a part of it came crashing down.</i>

00:04:40.290 --> 00:04:43.880
<i>Doesn't that mean it's extremely crucial?</i>

00:04:48.240 --> 00:04:51.640
<i>Life with intelligence but 
no love will never expand?</i>

00:04:51.640 --> 00:04:54.840
<i>W-Wait, why does it have to expand, anyway?</i>

00:04:55.400 --> 00:04:57.330
<i>Huh? For such a sweet reason?</i>

00:04:57.330 --> 00:04:59.340
<i>But God doesn't exist.</i>

00:04:59.340 --> 00:05:00.610
<i>"End of Chapter One"?</i>

00:05:00.610 --> 00:05:02.100
<i>Where's Chapter Two?</i>

00:05:02.590 --> 00:05:05.260
<i>Very well, I'll go...</i>

00:05:11.330 --> 00:05:14.520
<i>Even higher, to see for myself.</i>

00:05:22.970 --> 00:05:23.810
Ow.

00:05:29.540 --> 00:05:32.200
So this is as far as a human can go.

00:05:32.650 --> 00:05:34.520
I won't be able to understand any more.

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:36.990
But maybe it's because of that

00:05:36.990 --> 00:05:38.560
that I can have hope.

00:05:39.290 --> 00:05:41.170
I want to see Kagari.

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:49.400
Oh...

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:52.260
I went too far and flew too high,

00:05:52.930 --> 00:05:54.450
so now I can't go back?

00:05:58.840 --> 00:06:00.980
Isn't this Kagari's?

00:06:06.890 --> 00:06:07.880
Is that...

00:06:09.310 --> 00:06:10.430
Kagari's beacon?

00:06:18.920 --> 00:06:20.420
I was so cold.

00:06:20.420 --> 00:06:22.440
But I'm warm now.

00:06:24.770 --> 00:06:26.240
You saved me, didn't you?

00:06:28.350 --> 00:06:30.580
No matter where one is, one can always find

00:06:30.980 --> 00:06:33.310
a lodestar that shows the way.

00:06:33.730 --> 00:06:34.580
That's you...

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:37.910
What I'm doing isn't pointless anymore.

00:06:39.600 --> 00:06:41.670
I want to help you with your research.

00:06:46.150 --> 00:06:48.540
<i>The theory of life that Kagari's researching</i>

00:06:48.540 --> 00:06:52.620
<i>is a flowchart shaped like a giant tree.</i>

00:06:52.620 --> 00:06:56.310
<i>It contains information on the 
very beginnings of the world,</i>

00:06:56.310 --> 00:06:58.430
<i>in which the primal form of life</i>

00:06:58.430 --> 00:07:01.190
Aurora

00:06:58.700 --> 00:07:01.190
<i>is called "Aurora."</i>

00:07:07.380 --> 00:07:09.620
<i>"Aurora," originating from 
the familiar Latin "aurora,"</i>

00:07:09.620 --> 00:07:13.440
<i>is used here to mean "life" 
or "omnipotent power,"</i>

00:07:13.440 --> 00:07:16.080
<i>but it can be translated 
to a more fitting word.</i>

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:17.620
Miracle

00:07:16.610 --> 00:07:17.620
<i>"Miracle."</i>

00:07:19.340 --> 00:07:20.930
<i>The universe is a cruel place.</i>

00:07:20.930 --> 00:07:24.670
<i>The chances of life appearing 
anywhere are extremely close to zero.</i>

00:07:24.670 --> 00:07:25.590
<i>In other words—</i>

00:07:26.040 --> 00:07:28.340
<i>Actually, scratch that.</i>

00:07:28.340 --> 00:07:32.840
<i>Aurora, the power residing in our 
planet, aids the creation of life.</i>

00:07:33.190 --> 00:07:35.950
<i>And, for some reason, it creates the Key...</i>

00:07:36.530 --> 00:07:38.890
<i>To destroy the civilization it gave birth to.</i>

00:07:41.510 --> 00:07:43.360
Guess it was too much to take in at once...

00:07:51.520 --> 00:07:53.920
<i>If the giant tree represents the world,</i>

00:07:54.870 --> 00:07:58.290
<i>then do the withered branches 
represent ones that have ended?</i>

00:08:00.500 --> 00:08:04.040
Nothing like a piping hot coffee 
to get your mind off things.

00:08:08.010 --> 00:08:09.460
This is myyum!

00:08:09.460 --> 00:08:11.880
Wait, why does that sound familiar?

00:08:15.240 --> 00:08:17.560
Just my imagination?

00:08:35.570 --> 00:08:37.570
Now this is a surprise.

00:08:40.020 --> 00:08:43.330
You aren't the Key, are you?

00:08:44.370 --> 00:08:45.170
The Key?

00:08:48.940 --> 00:08:52.160
<i>That was something I'm very familiar with...</i>

00:08:53.260 --> 00:08:54.300
<i>A monster...</i>

00:09:00.710 --> 00:09:03.270
How unusual to not see Kagari here.

00:09:08.690 --> 00:09:11.150
<i>The theory of life contains 
a chronicle of evolution.</i>

00:09:12.150 --> 00:09:15.840
<i>To maintain the ecosystem 
Aurora gave birth to,</i>

00:09:15.840 --> 00:09:17.870
<i>the process of evolution was necessary.</i>

00:09:18.700 --> 00:09:22.120
<i>Eventually, humans came into 
existence and built a civilization.</i>

00:09:22.740 --> 00:09:24.750
<i>And when it reached that stage,</i>

00:09:24.750 --> 00:09:27.880
<i>the tree rapidly branched out.</i>

00:09:29.210 --> 00:09:31.250
What are these things?

00:09:35.410 --> 00:09:37.290
What was that?

00:09:40.530 --> 00:09:41.470
Could it be...

00:09:46.200 --> 00:09:48.310
I know all of these.

00:09:48.970 --> 00:09:52.930
Don't tell me... Each of these branches

00:09:52.930 --> 00:09:55.600
is a unique path humanity 
could potentially take?

00:09:59.290 --> 00:10:01.810
<i>The tree consumes a massive amount of energy</i>

00:10:01.810 --> 00:10:04.000
<i>and creates countless branches—worlds.</i>

00:10:04.650 --> 00:10:06.650
<i>Unlike the trunk, the 
branches are thin and frail,</i>

00:10:06.650 --> 00:10:08.170
<i>and they wither in the end...</i>

00:10:09.720 --> 00:10:10.700
<i>They die out.</i>

00:10:12.060 --> 00:10:13.430
What's the meaning of this?

00:10:13.780 --> 00:10:15.180
Is this Kagari's will?

00:10:15.590 --> 00:10:17.080
Or the planet's?

00:10:17.810 --> 00:10:18.720
Why?

00:10:20.260 --> 00:10:21.160
Crap!

00:10:21.160 --> 00:10:23.560
The information is all 
flowing into me at once...

00:10:32.490 --> 00:10:34.990
"Life." A mysterious concept.

00:10:35.470 --> 00:10:38.110
The chances of its natural occurrence

00:10:38.110 --> 00:10:40.340
from the beginning to the end of the universe

00:10:40.340 --> 00:10:43.230
are 0.0000000000...

00:10:43.230 --> 00:10:47.050
"Aurora." An energy source 
that facilitates life.

00:10:47.410 --> 00:10:50.350
It is highly sensitive to gravity,

00:10:50.350 --> 00:10:52.360
and it is found combined 
with the surface resources

00:10:52.360 --> 00:10:54.070
of planets with heavy mass...

00:10:54.070 --> 00:10:56.770
"Re-evolution." The recycling of life.

00:10:57.320 --> 00:10:59.300
When Aurora reaches critical concentration,

00:10:59.300 --> 00:11:01.050
massive tremors occur,

00:11:01.050 --> 00:11:03.630
with intelligent life at the epicenter...

00:11:03.630 --> 00:11:04.920
What is all this?

00:11:05.650 --> 00:11:06.830
"What is all this?"

00:11:06.830 --> 00:11:10.590
This theory does not have a 
valid response to this question.

00:11:10.590 --> 00:11:12.400
What the hell is life?!

00:11:13.100 --> 00:11:14.860
"What the hell is life?"

00:11:14.860 --> 00:11:17.360
Cannot answer this question.

00:11:17.360 --> 00:11:20.350
The reader's mind could be destroyed.

00:11:20.350 --> 00:11:22.070
Just tell me!

00:11:22.490 --> 00:11:24.080
"Just tell me!"

00:11:24.080 --> 00:11:29.700
This theory is not responsible for 
any damage the reader might receive

00:11:29.700 --> 00:11:31.570
by accessing the relevant data.

00:11:31.570 --> 00:11:33.200
Do you agree?

00:11:33.200 --> 00:11:35.420
Check the appropriate box.

00:11:35.420 --> 00:11:36.920
Yes

00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:38.170
Kagari-chan will take no responsibility 
for whatever happens, okay?!

00:11:38.170 --> 00:11:38.590
<b>Planetary Spirit</b>

00:11:39.180 --> 00:11:44.430
<b>Planetary Spirit</b>

00:11:39.180 --> 00:11:44.430
<b>Top Secret Item / Under Restriction /

00:12:08.830 --> 00:12:09.910
Sorry.

00:12:10.570 --> 00:12:12.700
I was too careless.

00:12:15.530 --> 00:12:17.020
Canned coffee, huh?

00:12:19.850 --> 00:12:22.170
Yeah, I remember this, too.

00:12:33.060 --> 00:12:34.520
<i>I see.</i>

00:12:34.520 --> 00:12:35.940
<i>So that's how it is.</i>

00:12:36.490 --> 00:12:40.300
<i>Kagari isn't researching 
a way to destroy life.</i>

00:12:40.780 --> 00:12:45.200
<i>She's been looking for a 
way for life to survive.</i>

00:12:45.970 --> 00:12:47.820
<i>The reason the Key ends the world</i>

00:12:48.010 --> 00:12:51.010
<i>is to start a re-evolution before 
the planet's resources run out.</i>

00:12:51.200 --> 00:12:55.060
<i>It's a manifestation of the planet's 
desperate attempt to survive.</i>

00:12:55.850 --> 00:12:59.400
<i>I saw worlds in which the Key was 
killed, and the Salvation was averted.</i>

00:13:00.530 --> 00:13:04.110
<i>But they all, without exception, burned 
through all of Earth's resources</i>

00:13:04.670 --> 00:13:06.200
<i>and fell into ruin anyway.</i>

00:13:08.500 --> 00:13:12.050
<i>So even you, with all your intelligence, 
have run into a brick wall, huh?</i>

00:13:12.440 --> 00:13:14.180
<i>Is there no way out?</i>

00:13:23.180 --> 00:13:27.500
<i>Kagari must be a system created to 
explore all the possibilities.</i>

00:13:27.870 --> 00:13:29.460
<i>Nothing but a natural phenomenon.</i>

00:13:29.870 --> 00:13:30.840
<i>But even if she is,</i>

00:13:31.240 --> 00:13:33.370
<i>and even if no one does it,</i>

00:13:33.730 --> 00:13:36.140
<i>I want to protect this 
delicate little phenomenon.</i>

00:13:36.630 --> 00:13:37.870
<i>That's how I feel.</i>

00:13:44.430 --> 00:13:47.570
You need a break and a change 
of pace every now and then.

00:14:10.750 --> 00:14:13.520
It's like the entire town 
has sunk into the ocean.

00:14:14.690 --> 00:14:16.890
The trick to taking breathers during exams

00:14:16.890 --> 00:14:19.210
is to forget all about studying

00:14:19.210 --> 00:14:21.290
and do something completely unrelated.

00:14:21.570 --> 00:14:25.510
I bet doing the same thing forever 
makes your mind go stiff.

00:14:25.760 --> 00:14:28.800
And it will eventually break 
if you keep pushing yourself.

00:14:31.590 --> 00:14:33.310
You finally looked up.

00:14:33.820 --> 00:14:34.710
All right.

00:14:34.710 --> 00:14:36.270
Let's do something more befitting a date.

00:14:41.750 --> 00:14:44.420
Maybe it's because I touched 
your theory and learned a lot.

00:14:44.960 --> 00:14:46.900
It seems I can do stuff like this now.

00:14:49.600 --> 00:14:52.160
Will you give me the pleasure 
of dancing with you?

00:15:10.390 --> 00:15:12.680
It's a bit lonely being the only ones here.

00:15:16.720 --> 00:15:19.150
We're the center of attention now.

00:15:52.830 --> 00:15:53.720
There!

00:15:59.820 --> 00:16:01.160
Sorry, sorry.

00:16:05.410 --> 00:16:06.420
Kagari...

00:16:11.410 --> 00:16:12.200
Kagari?

00:16:15.320 --> 00:16:17.330
This is hostility...

00:16:17.690 --> 00:16:19.220
Malice, hatred.

00:16:19.230 --> 00:16:21.970
Only humans would possess those feelings.

00:16:23.300 --> 00:16:26.220
<i>Humans who want to kill Kagari, the Key.</i>

00:16:26.680 --> 00:16:27.590
<i>Is it Guardian?</i>

00:16:29.910 --> 00:16:31.200
Wait, this aura...

00:16:31.680 --> 00:16:32.970
Stay back, Kagari.

00:16:38.600 --> 00:16:40.260
So it was a monster!

00:16:46.430 --> 00:16:48.550
<i>I can't complete my swing?!</i>

00:16:50.990 --> 00:16:51.820
Not on my watch!

00:16:54.110 --> 00:16:54.990
Kagari!

00:17:15.350 --> 00:17:16.720
What was that?

00:17:18.720 --> 00:17:20.350
<i>Who sent it?</i>

00:17:22.200 --> 00:17:24.490
<i>Read the information.</i>

00:17:27.020 --> 00:17:28.430
Kashima Sakura?

00:17:29.170 --> 00:17:31.270
Gaia's Saint?!

00:17:31.920 --> 00:17:32.860
<i>No way!</i>

00:17:33.450 --> 00:17:35.130
<i>Are you saying she's interfering</i>

00:17:35.130 --> 00:17:37.160
<i>with this place from one 
of the branch worlds?!</i>

00:17:37.400 --> 00:17:40.300
<i>Kashima Sakura hated everything.</i>

00:17:40.680 --> 00:17:42.690
<i>Not just human society,</i>

00:17:42.690 --> 00:17:45.660
<i>but the entire system of life.</i>

00:17:46.200 --> 00:17:48.460
<i>Does she desire ruin that much?</i>

00:17:49.160 --> 00:17:51.590
<i>The branch worlds aren't enough...</i>

00:17:51.590 --> 00:17:54.800
<i>She wants to eradicate all 
possibility of survival?</i>

00:17:57.940 --> 00:17:58.800
Kagari.

00:18:01.300 --> 00:18:02.440
I'll protect you.

00:18:02.790 --> 00:18:06.930
I bet that's why I was sent here.

00:18:15.530 --> 00:18:16.580
<i>What was I...</i>

00:18:17.440 --> 00:18:20.540
<i>What was I just trying to do with my hands?!</i>

00:18:25.950 --> 00:18:28.210
She's sending in a bunch of monsters?

00:18:37.810 --> 00:18:41.090
Just how big a freak is Kashima Sakura?!

00:18:46.050 --> 00:18:47.410
<i>I knew it.</i>

00:18:47.410 --> 00:18:49.940
<i>My body feels sluggish when 
I'm up against monsters.</i>

00:18:49.940 --> 00:18:50.900
<i>Oh...</i>

00:18:50.900 --> 00:18:52.110
<i>I see what's going on!</i>

00:18:52.510 --> 00:18:58.050
Damn it all!

00:19:13.200 --> 00:19:16.880
Piss off already!

00:19:44.950 --> 00:19:46.500
Kashima Sakura.

00:19:46.500 --> 00:19:48.330
I'm Tennouji Kotarou.

00:19:48.800 --> 00:19:50.700
Ever since I found myself in this place,

00:19:50.700 --> 00:19:52.870
I've been trying to figure out why.

00:19:53.660 --> 00:19:54.840
Until a few moments ago,

00:19:54.840 --> 00:19:57.650
I thought I was summoned to protect Kagari.

00:19:57.650 --> 00:20:00.870
But your attack helped me realize the truth.

00:20:01.430 --> 00:20:03.680
I wanted to save everyone at first.

00:20:04.050 --> 00:20:06.300
But that proved impossible,

00:20:06.680 --> 00:20:11.180
so all I could do was pick one 
out of countless possibilities.

00:20:11.570 --> 00:20:14.560
And in pretty much all of them,
the choice I made

00:20:14.560 --> 00:20:16.380
led to the loss of something...

00:20:17.060 --> 00:20:18.050
Kagari.

00:20:19.770 --> 00:20:23.500
Just as the Key always showed up as Kagari,

00:20:23.500 --> 00:20:27.340
I, too, showed up as her counterpart.

00:20:27.840 --> 00:20:28.930
I swear...

00:20:29.270 --> 00:20:32.100
I thought I was protecting someone, 
but I was actually her killer.

00:20:32.530 --> 00:20:34.470
But I've changed.

00:20:34.470 --> 00:20:36.820
I want to protect Kagari now.

00:20:36.820 --> 00:20:38.460
It's thanks to you.

00:20:38.460 --> 00:20:40.700
Because you took my position,

00:20:40.700 --> 00:20:43.170
I've been freed from that role.

00:20:44.040 --> 00:20:46.100
I thank you, Kashima Sakura.

00:20:46.580 --> 00:20:48.710
And I'm hereby declaring war...

00:20:48.710 --> 00:20:49.970
As of now,

00:20:50.320 --> 00:20:51.520
I'm your enemy!

00:20:53.260 --> 00:20:54.610
This is a crucial juncture.

00:20:54.610 --> 00:20:57.250
Your research is approaching completion.

00:20:57.250 --> 00:21:00.840
That's why Kashima Sakura sent her monsters.

00:21:01.240 --> 00:21:03.940
Listen, you're on the right track here.

00:21:04.380 --> 00:21:06.870
You must do everything you 
can to reach your goal

00:21:06.870 --> 00:21:09.070
and find hope for life.

00:21:09.070 --> 00:21:09.870
And to that end,

00:21:10.410 --> 00:21:11.870
I want to get some help.

00:21:11.870 --> 00:21:15.000
As much as I hate to admit it, 
I can't protect you alone.

00:21:16.920 --> 00:21:18.270
What will I do?

00:21:18.270 --> 00:21:19.380
That's obvious.

00:21:26.950 --> 00:21:28.920
Get everyone together 
for one last club activity.

00:21:34.520 --> 00:21:35.770
So you came,

00:21:36.550 --> 00:21:37.430
Kotori.

00:21:38.010 --> 00:21:38.670
Yeah.

00:21:39.040 --> 00:21:40.970
I'm here, Kotarou-kun,

00:21:41.390 --> 00:21:42.780
to help you out.

00:21:44.280 --> 00:21:45.650
Hey there, bro.

00:21:45.650 --> 00:21:48.910
Looks like we've got the 
coolest gig waiting for us.

00:21:50.930 --> 00:21:53.410
What's wrong? You're the 
one who summoned them.

00:21:53.410 --> 00:21:55.800
No, what I wished for was...

00:21:55.800 --> 00:21:57.570
You're late, Tennouji.

00:22:00.540 --> 00:22:01.630
Yoshino.

00:22:02.110 --> 00:22:03.550
You'll help me?

00:22:03.850 --> 00:22:05.150
No.

00:22:05.150 --> 00:22:07.510
I'm just doing what I want.

00:22:07.510 --> 00:22:09.300
Don't get too cocky.

00:22:10.750 --> 00:22:12.790
You're one to talk, punk.

00:22:22.590 --> 00:22:25.130
Sheesh, took you long enough.

00:22:25.130 --> 00:22:25.920
Kotarou.

00:22:25.920 --> 00:22:27.210
Hey there.

00:22:27.210 --> 00:22:29.930
You call us here and then show up late?

00:22:29.930 --> 00:22:30.820
Who do you think you are?

00:22:31.450 --> 00:22:33.570
<i>I wished for the ideal 
world I failed to realize.</i>

00:22:33.570 --> 00:22:35.570
<i>Promises I failed to keep.</i>

00:22:36.060 --> 00:22:39.210
<i>I dragged them out in such 
a do-or-die situation.</i>

00:22:39.730 --> 00:22:43.590
<i>Am I just playing out my 
own selfish desires here?</i>

00:22:44.170 --> 00:22:45.860
You're wrong, Kotarou-kun.

00:22:48.750 --> 00:22:50.470
We are who we've always been...

00:22:51.470 --> 00:22:54.400
Just like you, okay?

00:22:55.050 --> 00:22:56.090
Guys...

00:23:00.850 --> 00:23:03.240
The occult club is back in action!
